## Step 5, the print check and the judge copies (0 USD)

- The print check reads the sharp metadata of each file. All 3 print files hold 2480 x 3508 px, RGB,
  with 3 channels and no alpha. The check passes.
- The native color file holds 1280 x 1920 px, with a ratio of 0.6667. The target ratio 2480 / 3508 is
  0.7069. The reframe function of the muse tool returns the buffer unchanged, because the native
  width is under the target width. The resize then uses the default fit `cover`. It scales by 1.9375
  to 2480 x 3720 px and trims 212 px from the top and 212 px from the bottom of the scaled picture.
  That is 2.85 percent of the height at each end. The crop does not trim the sides. D5 expected a
  side trim, so the judge reads the print as it is.
